This product builds on third-party software and models that keep their own licenses: COLMAP
(BSD-3-Clause, via pycolmap), OpenMVS (AGPL-3.0, run as separate programs; in the Docker image with
its source in /usr/share/doc/openmvs), three.js and three-mesh-bvh (MIT, bundled in
src/motiongrammetry/web/static/vendor), xatlas (MIT) and pybind11 (BSD-3-Clause), compiled into the
xatlas Python package, the subject segmentation models (MIT / Apache-2.0), the
optional VGGT (VGGT License; its weights CC BY-NC 4.0, non-commercial) and many Python packages.
The full list with every license text: the About page of the app, or `mg notices`.

The example objects in the help page's screenshots and in benchmarks/ come from Meta's uCO3D dataset
(Liu et al., 2025, https://uco3d.github.io), licensed CC BY 4.0.
